# refused (it said "expected ';', got '['" in a const fn, "expected ';' after a const's value" in a const's value,
# "expected ']'" in an array size). The evaluator stops past the `]`, so a context that ends there (an enum
# member's `,`, an array size's `]`, a case label's `:`) is left in sync. A const fn's own frame entries keep
