# first statement — and so the declarations after it (`_dl_fill`) — is known: `var arr: i64[E.B];` with `enum E` after
# the first statement was "unknown name 'E' in a const context", printed before the enum's own error. There a name a
# later zone declaration declares (valid, declared after its use) and one declared after the first statement (refused)
# look alike, so the report of a name some later declaration declares (`_declared_later`) is held (`_ce_zpend`: its
# token, its name), counted and latched as the printed one is, and said by `_ce_zflush` at the end of pass 1's tail walk,
# once every late declaration's names are in: a refused declaration's name is dropped (its one error stands), any other
